{"name":"Hair dye / bleaching","deep":true,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Dyeing_hair_purple.png/960px-Dyeing_hair_purple.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dyeing_hair_purple.png","caption":"Dyeing hair purple","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},"mentions":17,"casual":{"lead":["Hair dye and bleach change hair color on the spot: lighter, darker, or gray covered. In style circles they are used to change contrast with the skin and eyes and give a visibly new look. Reports say 50 to 80 percent of women in the US, Europe and Japan have used hair dye.","Permanent dye and bleach use an oxidizer and an alkaline agent such as ammonia to open the hair cuticle; bleach oxidizes melanin to lighten, while dye deposits color. Lower-strength dyes coat or lightly penetrate the hair without lightening. The techniques are well established, though no studies test whether coloring improves attractiveness."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["People color at a salon or at home, with bleach followed by toner for lighter shades and a permanent or semi-permanent dye for darker or natural-looking color. Roots need touching up as hair grows, and bleached hair is usually given extra conditioning."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Reported risks are skin irritation, PPD allergy, hair breakage, skin staining and unexpected color. Studies linking dye to cancer are limited and inconsistent, and the EU restricts about 45 hair dye chemicals."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Dyeing_hair_purple.png/960px-Dyeing_hair_purple.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/dc/Dyeing_hair_purple.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Dyeing hair purple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","creator":"WhatamIdoing","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dyeing_hair_purple.png","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Hair_bleaching_toner_diagram.svg/960px-Hair_bleaching_toner_diagram.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ad/Hair_bleaching_toner_diagram.svg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Hair bleaching toner diagram","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","creator":"Gogolplex","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hair_bleaching_toner_diagram.svg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"}],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"At-home vs In-office Bleaching: An Updated Systematic Review and Meta-analysis.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40485133/","source":"Operative dentistry","year":2025,"cites":null,"kind":"Systematic Review"},{"title":"Retinopathy Associated With Hair Dye.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39264642/","source":"JAMA ophthalmology","year":2024,"cites":null,"kind":null},{"title":"Intracoronal tooth bleaching - A review and treatment guidelines.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37975331/","source":"Australian dental journal","year":2023,"cites":null,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Prognosis in home dental bleaching: a systematic review.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37273018/","source":"Clinical oral investigations","year":2023,"cites":null,"kind":"Systematic Review"},{"title":"Effect of Tooth Bleach on Dentin Fatigue Resistance in Situ.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37881145/","source":"Operative dentistry","year":2023,"cites":null,"kind":"Randomized Controlled Trial"},{"title":"Present status and future directions - Managing discoloured teeth.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35188275/","source":"International endodontic journal","year":2022,"cites":null,"kind":