r skin the official guide the truth about skin bleaching","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/how-to-bleach-your-skin-the-official-guide-the-truth-about-skin-bleaching.1669648/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251228040229/https://looksmax.org/threads/how-to-bleach-your-skin-the-official-guide-the-truth-about-skin-bleaching.1669648/"},{"title":"why do curries think bleaching their skin will change their dravidian physiognomy","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/why-do-curries-think-bleaching-their-skin-will-change-their-dravidian-physiognomy.1444268/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250517184909/https://looksmax.org/threads/why-do-curries-think-bleaching-their-skin-will-change-their-dravidian-physiognomy.1444268/"},{"title":"anal bleaching guide 2024 gtfih","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/anal-bleaching-guide-2024-gtfih.1103102/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240804210457/https://looksmax.org/threads/anal-bleaching-guide-2024-gtfih.1103102/"},{"title":"best natural hair dye","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/best-natural-hair-dye.1028298/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240506174248/https://looksmax.org/threads/best-natural-hair-dye.1028298/"},{"title":"anyone tried skin bleaching","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/anyone-tried-skin-bleaching.882818/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20231127152851/https://looksmax.org/threads/anyone-tried-skin-bleaching.882818/"},{"title":"natural hair bleaching a few shades","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/natural-hair-bleaching-a-few-shades.603223/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20221113203053/https://looksmax.org/threads/natural-hair-bleaching-a-few-shades.603223/"},{"title":"how do i know if black or dark brown hair dye will suit me best","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/how-do-i-know-if-black-or-dark-brown-hair-dye-will-suit-me-best.541226/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220802040047/https://looksmax.org/threads/how-do-i-know-if-black-or-dark-brown-hair-dye-will-suit-me-best.541226/"},{"title":"success professional teeth bleaching results","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/success-professional-teeth-bleaching-results.267235/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20211118164911/https://looksmax.org/threads/success-professional-teeth-bleaching-results.267235/"},{"title":"What Business is it of Yours Where I'm From, Friendo?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/what-business-is-it-of-yours-where-im-from-friendo/208666","site":"T Nation · 2469 posts · 2015"},{"title":"Let's Try This: Grneyes' s Log","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/lets-try-this-grneyes-s-log/147176","site":"T Nation · 863 posts · 2010"},{"title":"A Black Spiderman?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/a-black-spiderman/150187","site":"T Nation · 136 posts · 2010"},{"title":"Lifting with Long Hair","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/lifting-with-long-hair/122549","site":"T Nation · 92 posts · 2009"},{"title":"Meaty Guilt","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/meaty-guilt/43690","site":"T Nation · 30 posts · 2005"},{"title":"Steroids and Hair Color","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/steroids-and-hair-color/209910","site":"T Nation · 6 posts · 2015"},{"title":"skin whitening bleaching","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/skin-whitening-bleaching.54419/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220817110102/https://looksmax.org/threads/skin-whitening-bleaching.54419/"}],"news":[],"social":[{"title":"Breast Cancer Linked to Permanent Hair Dye and Chemical Hair Straighteners","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=21707312","site":"Hacker News","score":123,"comments":43,"year":2019},{"title":"Hair dye and chemical straightener use and breast cancer risk (2019)","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=36836866","site":"Hacker News","score":89,"comments":30,"year":2023},{"title":"Multifunctional Graphene Hair Dye (2018)","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=22976643","site":"Hacker News","score":39,"comments":4,"year":2020}],"web":[{"title":"Hair coloring - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hair_coloring"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Style & presentation","chain":["Hair color changed","Different contrast with skin and eyes","Visibly new look"],"effect":"direct","text":"Bleaching hair lighter or dyeing it darker changes your contrast with your skin and eyes and covers gray, and the new color is visible immediately. Hair coloring is a well-established cosmetic method used by a large share of adults."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Hair coloring changes the color of head hair, typically to cover gray, change a look or restore color after bleaching or sun exposure. In looksmaxxing and style discussions it is raised as a way to alter contrast, for example bleaching hair lighter or dyeing it darker. Reports say 50 to 80 percent of women in the US, Europe and Japan have used hair dye.[1]","Bleaching lightens hair by oxidizing melanin, using hydrogen peroxide with an alkaline agent such as ammonia.[1] Documented risks include skin irritation, allergy, hair breakage and unexpected color. Studies on hair dye and cancer risk are described as limited and inconsistent.[1]"],"infobox":[["Type","Style / grooming meta"],["Main methods","Permanent, demi-permanent, semi-permanent, temporary dyes; bleaching"],["Typical bleach strength","About 6% peroxide at home, up to 12% in salons[1]"],["Key risk","Allergy to p-phenylenediamine (PPD), breakage[1]"],["Evidence level","Moderate (as a cosmetic technique)"]],"sections":[{"h":"Types of coloring","paras":["Permanent dye uses ammonia and an oxidizing developer to open the hair cuticle and deposit color in the cortex. Demi-permanent dye uses a lower peroxide level and cannot lighten hair, and semi-permanent dye, which can still contain PPD, lasts about 4 to 8 shampoos. Temporary products wash out in one shampoo.[1]","Vivid or fashion colors contain tint but no developer, so on dark hair they usually require bleaching first.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Bleaching","paras":["Bleaching breaks down melanin by oxidation, releasing oxygen gas. Bleached hair can turn brassy or yellow, and toners and purple shampoos are used to correct undertones.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"History","paras":["Hair dye recipes appear in Assyrian herbals from about 2177 BCE, and the Egyptian Ebers Papyrus (about 1550 BCE) describes dyeing gray hair. Diodorus Siculus described Celtic peoples bleaching hair with lime.[1] Perkin's discovery of mauveine in 1856 launched synthetic dyes, Eugene Schueller is credited with the first synthetic hair dye in 1907, and Schwarzkopf launched a home color product in 1947.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Reported risks","paras":["Dye can cause skin irritation, allergic reactions, hair breakage and skin staining. PPD-based dyes have been controversial, symptoms can appear hours to a day later, and manufacturers recommend patch testing, which some European dermatologists advise against for self-testing.[1]","The IARC has reported that some hair dyes and ingredients can be considered mutagenic or carcinogenic. Studies have associated hair dye with certain cancers, and a 2017 meta-analysis suggested roughly 20 percent higher breast cancer risk among users, but evidence overall is described as limited and inconsistent.[1] The EU restricts about 45 chemicals in hair dyes.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found testing hair color change as a means of improving attractiveness. Epidemiological studies on hair dye use and health include the Copenhagen City Heart Study (2016, 7,684 women followed for 37 years) and a 2018 meta-analysis on breast cancer risk.[1]"],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"c. 1550 BCE","event":"Ebers Papyrus describes dyeing gray hair.[1]"},{"year":"1856","event":"Perkin discovers mauveine, the first synthetic dye.[1]"},{"year":"1907","event":"Eugene Schueller is credited with the first synthetic hair dye.[1]"},{"year":"1947","event":"Schwarzkopf launches the home color product Poly Color.[1]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Hair coloring","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hair_coloring","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[{"title":"Hair coloring","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hair_coloring","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"kind":null}],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"hair dye","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/hair-dye.1778423/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260113090619/https://looksmax.org/threads/hair-dye.1778423/"},{"title":"hair dye","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/hair-dye.1180666/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20241214095548/https://looksmax.org/threads/hair-dye.1180666/"},{"title":"Cope bleaching my hair right now.","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/bleaching-my-hair-right-now.563547/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220924091450/https://looksmax.org/threads/bleaching-my-hair-right-now.563547/"},{"title":"hair dye suggestions","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/hair-dye-suggestions.486037/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220422181625/https://looksmax.org/threads/hair-dye-suggestions.486037/"},{"title":"hair dye and ideal colouring","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/hair-dye-and-ideal-colouring.5793/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20221208083842/https://looksmax.org/threads/hair-dye-and-ideal-colouring.5793/"},{"title":"did skin bleaching ascend asdvek","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/did-skin-bleaching-ascend-asdvek.1790159/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251228173331/https://looksmax.org/threads/did-skin-bleaching-ascend-asdvek.1790159/"},{"title":"asdveks bleaching progress","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/asdv